<article class="env-lemma" id="837C14">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/837C14">Lemma <span data-tag="837C14">6.5.2.10</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be an $\infty $-topos, let $L: \calX \rightarrow \calX ^{\wedge }$ be a left adjoint to the inclusion, and let $X \in \calX $ be such that $LX$ is an $\infty $-connective object of $\calX ^{\wedge }$. Then $LX$ is a final object of $\calX ^{\wedge }$. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      For each $n < \infty $, we have equivalences 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[ 1_{\calX } \simeq \tau _{\leq n}^{\calX ^{\wedge }} LX \simeq L \tau _{\leq n}^{\calX } X\simeq \tau _{\leq n}^{\calX } X \]
</div>
    <p>
       where the first is because of our hypothesis that $LX$ is $\infty $-connective, the second is given by Proposition <a href="/tag/7751D7" data-tag="7751D7">5.5.6.28</a>, and the third by Lemma <a href="/tag/B67D73" data-tag="B67D73">6.5.2.9</a>. It follows that $X$ is an $\infty $-connective object of $\calX $, so that $LX$ is a final object of $\calX ^{\wedge }$ by construction. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>